<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basil I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">811–886</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Basil the Macedonian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Basil I was Byzantine emperor from 867 to 886 and founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-dynasty">Macedonian dynasty</a>, which ruled for nearly two centuries. A peasant from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> who rose as a favourite of Michael III, he had his rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barda">Bardas</a> and then Michael himself murdered. He destroyed the Paulician state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divrigi">Tephrike</a>, recovered ground in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and began a revision of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> completed by his son Leo VI.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basil-i.jpg" alt="Basil I" width="320" height="503" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_Emperor_Basil_I.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
